{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-analyzer-002-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/Analyzer/BaselineFilterTests.cs", "line": 338, "method": "Apply_IsDeterministic", "category": "T1", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Analyzer/BaselineFilter.cs:262 and :280; replace SortedKeys(...) with raw Dictionary key order -> stays green", "what_it_asserts": "Two identical in-process Apply runs produce the same sorted finding projection.", "why_weak": "Both Run() calls execute in one process over one insertion order, so Dictionary/HashSet enumeration is already identical; deleting the SortedKeys ordering that the determinism guarantee rests on does not red it.", "proposed_action": "Assert the emitted meta-finding order directly: build entries whose insertion order differs from the (ruleId, target, sectionIndex, digest) ordinal order and pin the expected STALE-ENTRY / MULTI-MATCH sequence.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-analyzer-002-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/Analyzer/BaselineFilterTests.cs", "line": 89, "method": "Key_SameFindingTwice_IsStable", "category": "T1", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Analyzer/BaselineFilter.cs:66; stub KeyOf to return default(BaselineKey) -> stays green", "what_it_asserts": "KeyOf(f) equals KeyOf(f) for one Finding instance.", "why_weak": "A pure function compared against itself on the same argument; no implementation short of throwing can fail it. The named risk (a key component picking up run-to-run state) is not reachable from one call site.", "proposed_action": "Key two SEPARATE Finding instances carrying the same RuleId/Target/SectionIndex and structurally equal but numerically different messages, and assert equal keys; that pins both the digest mask and key stability.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
